    <ObjectList>
      <MultilingualText ID="100000" CompositionName="Comment">
        <ObjectList>
          <MultilingualTextItem ID="100001" CompositionName="Items">
            <AttributeList>
              <Culture>en-US</Culture>
              <Text>Dedicated startup-reset block (C-124/C-305/C-403), run once by the CPU on every restart (warm or cold), regardless of retentivity - non-retentivity is never relied on to clear state. Forces Step back to idle (C-118/C-119) on every stepped sequencer, clears every S/R-driven and transient-run-state bit named in the fix-wave-1 B-2 finding, and force-resets DB_PLC.Simulation (C-305). Genuine fault latches - iDB_MotorFwdRevSystem_Shredder.IO.FaultActive/FTR/FTS, iDB_PusherControl.IO.Blocked/EndTravelTimeoutFault/ParkedTimeoutFault/BothSwitchesFault, iDB_ShredderSequencer.IO.ShredderBlockedFault/DischargeConveyorTimeoutFault - are deliberately excluded per C-124's carve-out: a fault needing human acknowledgement (FaultReset) still needs it after a power cycle. Closes owner-questions B-2/D-1/Q-01 and doc 06 C-128 (no automatic restart after a stop or power event).</Text>
            </AttributeList>
          </MultilingualTextItem>
        </ObjectList>
      </MultilingualText>
